# Design & UX Workflow

Use the installed design skills for any UI work. Do not hand-roll generic styling.

## Skill routing (invoke before writing UI)

| Task | Skill to use |
| --- | --- |
| Choose aesthetic direction, style, palette, font pairing | `ui-ux-pro-max` |
| Build a distinctive page/hero that must not look templated | `frontend-design` |
| Critique, polish, or "make it better / bolder / quieter" | `impeccable` |
| Define tokens, spacing/typography scales, component specs | `design-system` |
| Add/organize reusable components with Tailwind theming | `shadcn` + `ui-styling` |
| Social/hero banners and brand visuals | `banner-design` |

## Portfolio design targets

- Aesthetic direction: run `ui-ux-pro-max` first, then implement with `frontend-design`.
- Design system: single brand color scale (see `brand` in `tailwind.config.ts`), one
  type pairing (e.g. Inter / Sora), a consistent spacing rhythm. Extend tokens there —
  do not scatter arbitrary hex values in components.
- Layout: mobile-first responsive; 8px spacing base; max-w-5xl content container (already set).
- Components: prefer accessible primitives; if adding a component library, use `shadcn`.
- Demos gallery: image-forward cards with hover elevation, consistent 16:10 aspect ratio.

## Quality bar (verify before calling UI done)

- Conformance: semantic HTML, keyboard-operable, visible focus rings, AA contrast.
- Motion: subtle, purposeful transitions (<=200ms) on interactive elements.
- No lorem/placeholder copy left in shipped UI; real name, links, and screenshots.

## Process

1. `ui-ux-pro-max` to plan direction + tokens (write decisions into `tailwind.config.ts`).
2. Implement with `frontend-design` / `shadcn` following existing structure.
3. `impeccable` to review and refine against the quality bar above.
